@startuml Sequence_7
hide footbox
title Scenario 7: Enemy Turn — Goblin Still Stunned, StunEffect Expires

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor       "User"                         as User
boundary    "ArenaBattleScreen"            as Screen
control     "GameApp\n<<ActionCallbacks>>" as App
control     "BattleEngine"                 as Engine
entity      "Goblin\n<<Enemy>>"            as Goblin
entity      "StunEffect\n<<StatusEffect>>" as Stun
entity      "GameState\n<<Static>>"        as State

note over User, State
  This is the enemy phase of the same executePlayerTurn() call as Scenario 6.
  Goblin's StunEffect has remainingTurns=1 entering this turn.
  Goblin skips again, and this time the StunEffect expires and is removed.
end note

' ── User Input (same round as Scenario 6) ──────────────────────
User -> Screen : clicks "Use Item" → selects Potion
note right of User
  Same user action that triggered Scenario 6.
  Shown here for continuity — enemy phase
  occurs in the same executePlayerTurn() call.
end note

Screen -> App : callbacks.onUseItem(itemIndex, targetIndex)
App -> Engine : executePlayerTurn(choice=3, targetIndex, potion, 1.0)
note right of App : choice=3 → Use Item branch (Scenario 6)

note over Engine
  Warrior phase: Potion used, healed 100 HP.
  (See Scenario 6 for player phase detail.)
  Now processing: Goblin (instanceof Enemy).
end note

' ── Goblin Phase — Stunned (final turn) ────────────────────────
Engine -> Goblin : beginTurn()
note over Goblin
  Iterates activeEffects → finds StunEffect (turns=1).
  Calls StunEffect.onTurnStart(goblin).
end note
Goblin -> Stun : onTurnStart(goblin)
note over Stun
  remainingTurns > 0
  remainingTurns-- (1 → 0)
  returns true → skip this turn
end note
Stun --> Goblin : true (skip turn)

Goblin -> Stun : isExpired()
note over Stun : remainingTurns = 0 → true
Stun --> Goblin : true

Goblin -> Stun : onExpire(goblin)
note over Goblin
  StunEffect.onExpire() is a no-op by default.
  Iterator removes StunEffect from activeEffects.
  canAct = false → returns false.
end note
Goblin --> Engine : false (cannot act)

note over Engine
  enemy.beginTurn() == false.
  Enemy AI strategy NOT executed.
  No attack TurnFrame added for Goblin.
  Goblin's activeEffects is now EMPTY.
  Goblin will attack normally next round.
end note

Engine -> Engine : sweepDeadEnemies()
note over Engine : Goblin hp > 0 — nothing removed.

' ── End of Round ───────────────────────────────────────────────
Engine -> State : checkEndCondition()
State --> Engine : 0 (continue)
Engine -> Engine : endRound()
note right of Engine
  round++
  warrior.decrementCooldownAfterTurn() → cooldown: 1→0
  GameState.newTurnOrder() — Goblin has NO StunEffect now
end note
Engine --> App : 0 (continue)

' ── Render Result ──────────────────────────────────────────────
App -> Engine : drainTurnFrames()
Engine --> App : [TurnFrame("Warrior uses Potion.")]\nnote: no Goblin attack frame
App -> Screen : render(ArenaViewState)
Screen --> User : updated battle screen\n(Goblin did not attack — Stun icon gone next round)

@enduml
